Subject: Baby Killing Assault Rifles - Glock 17

---
Most of the talk here has been about average to expensive handguns. Many people
on this list are quite well off financially, so price isn't that much of an 
issue. But some of us are less endowed, are cheap, or both, like myself. 
If someone is serious about defending their life it can be done at almost
any price. If it shoots and doesn't break, then it's usefull.
 It may not be very highbrow, but the Ruger P-85/89 (as used on the N.Y. subway
recently) will kill someone just as well as a gun several times it's ~$300
price. At smaller calibers there are even better bargains, although less than
a .380 is not recommended. 
 For example, I plan on getting a Lorcin for my girlfriend soon. It`s a rather
small .380 I expect to pay under $100 for, and it looks like something Batman
would keep in his glove compartment. A badguy/gal probably won't complain that
you aren't using a $600 SIG against them.
 My point is not to insult good high-priced guns and their owners, but to let
people know that life-saving tools can be affordable. Check around.

                       O Martin (the Bargainmiester)

P.S. I'll let you know if the Lorcin turns out to be crap.

